{"id": "EUVD-2026-81884", "enisaUuid": "a0552be8-1c86-32bc-bf5c-bef970c8c5c4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmodule/dups: Fix use-after-free in kmod_dup_req lifetime handling\n\nThe kmod dups code uses RCU to ensure that a kmod_dup_req instance is freed\nonly after it is no longer referenced. When releasing an instance, the\nkmod_dup_request_delete() function removes the kmod_dup_req from the\ndup_kmod_reqs list, waits via synchronize_rcu() and finally frees it.\nHowever, this doesn't work correctly because parallel users referencing the\ninstance in kmod_dup_request_exists_wait() don't enter an RCU read-side\ncritical section. This can result in a use-after-free.\n\nThe kmod_dup_request_exists_wait() function may need to hold a valid\nreference to a kmod_dup_req instance across a blocking wait until the\ncorresponding modprobe command completes. This makes it unsuitable for RCU.\n\nFix the issue by changing the lifecycle management of kmod_dup_req to use\nreference counting.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:49", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3205bd1f218053575589b14caf8df667f344134", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c85e0fb528e039aa8ea1e9c2a1f64347f990541", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2709aad7599f6fd957939b60f4a8323c8f08072", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd2396fc9684d2cfd3f3c3f09c79d6d9d725b0ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5eecb11b543f9f417bcf0dea239ff99c6af65dbd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90291", "GHSA-hjw3-fxm2-vph2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "24350da1-6fc3-35b4-88a1-4fd6eaafda8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "281df80a-29fa-3bb3-a483-dbb8d61cbfe4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8660484ed1cf3261e89e0bad94c6395597e87599 <a3205bd1f218053575589b14caf8df667f344134"}, {"id": "6d5f9dd9-27eb-31fd-b8fe-340ab3b29edd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "80893d8b-b9bc-3d6e-80f4-94282ab09417", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "906fc069-7dbc-3cf9-b5ed-cde17d7b5493", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8660484ed1cf3261e89e0bad94c6395597e87599 <2c85e0fb528e039aa8ea1e9c2a1f64347f990541"}, {"id": "9281f80d-e3f3-3ed2-b2fd-bbc37c79ee14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8660484ed1cf3261e89e0bad94c6395597e87599 <b2709aad7599f6fd957939b60f4a8323c8f08072"}, {"id": "9e59fe1e-34ce-3aa7-a6fc-f6cb0feba34c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "ad9885ea-cf29-3d5b-8117-320a198f517a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4"}, {"id": "b07f7fb5-3c29-32e2-aa94-8de64d8c450b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8660484ed1cf3261e89e0bad94c6395597e87599 <5eecb11b543f9f417bcf0dea239ff99c6af65dbd"}, {"id": "c3f2b9de-3693-3646-9f20-a1bd0c14a07c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8660484ed1cf3261e89e0bad94c6395597e87599 <cd2396fc9684d2cfd3f3c3f09c79d6d9d725b0ca"}, {"id": "d3cd30cc-3a21-3215-b435-75e78848cfd7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ea8e3f32-6673-3fa7-adab-8afcdb7811a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a0e4bbf3-527b-3377-bab4-6d825c42b881", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}